    "body": "Well, `YMODESW[IY]` also mutate the bit in `pc`... but that definitely means that it's got X-permission, and it can only be read back via `auipc` if it's `1` (hm)... Aaaanyway.  Phrasing it as \"may be a no-op\" is fine... that probably should say \"update this field therein\" or something, tho'.\r\n\r\nBUT!  I didn't notice the \"The value of rs1.tag does not affect the result\" over in `YMODEW`.  I... guess it's fine to have a strange bag of bits mutator instruction, but I'd feel more comfortable with it being a no-op on untagged `rs1`?",
